ABSTRACT.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 Red-eye is a common unwanted effect in digital photographs, especially when a camera flash is used. This project presents a simple red-eye reduction system developed using Python, OpenCV, NumPy, and Matplotlib. The system detects the unwanted red color in the eye region and reduces it using image-processing techniques. The corrected image is then displayed and saved as an output image. The project demonstrates basic concepts of color detection, masking, and image correction in digital image processing.
\f1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 1
\f0\b . INTRODUCTION.
\f1\b0 \
\
Red-eye is a common unwanted effect in digital photography. It happens when the camera flash reflects from the blood vessels at the back of the eye. This makes the eyes appear red in photographs.\
\
This project uses Python and OpenCV to detect the red area in the eye and reduce the unwanted red color. The aim is to make the photograph look more natural.\
\
2. 
\f0\b\fs28 OBJECTIVES.
\f1\b0 \

\fs24 \
\'95 To understand the red-eye effect in digital photography.\
\'95 To detect red-eye in a digital image.\
\'95 To reduce unwanted red color from the eyes.\
\'95 To improve the appearance of photographs.\
\'95 To learn basic image processing using Python and OpenCV.\
\'95 To develop a simple red-eye reduction system.\
\
3. 
\f0\b\fs28 PROBLEM STATEMENT\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
Red-eye is an unwanted effect that often appears in photographs taken with a camera flash. It can make the eyes look unnatural and reduce the quality of the photograph.\
\
Manually correcting red-eye can take time. Therefore, this project develops a simple image-processing system that detects unwanted red color in the eye region and reduces it automatically.\
\
4. 
\f0\b\fs28 BACKGROUND / LITERATURE REVIEW\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
Red-eye reduction is a common image-processing technique used in digital photography. The red-eye effect occurs when camera flash reflects from the blood vessels at the back of the eye.\
\
Image processing techniques can be used to identify the unwanted red color. HSV color space is useful for separating color information, while masking can help select the affected area. The red color can then be reduced to produce a more natural-looking photograph.\
\
5. 
\f0\b\fs28 METHODOLOGY
\f1\b0\fs24 \
The project follows these main steps:\
\
1. Input Image\
2. Image Reading using OpenCV\
3. Red-Eye Detection using HSV\
4. Region Selection\
5. Red-Eye Reduction\
6. Corrected Image\
7. Output Image\
\
The process starts by loading the photograph. The affected eye region is selected and converted to HSV color space. Red pixels are detected using a color mask. The unwanted red color is then reduced, and the corrected eye is placed back into the original image.\
\
6
