\

\f0\b 7.
\fs28  ALGORITHM
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\
1. Start\
2. Load the input image.\
3. Select the affected eye region.\
4. Convert the eye region to HSV color space.\
5. Detect red pixels.\
6. Remove small noise from the detected area.\
7. Reduce the extra red color.\
8. Put the corrected eye back into the image.\
9. Save the corrected image.\
10. Display the original, detected, and corrected images.\
11. Stop\
\
8. 
\f0\b\fs28 IMPLEMENTATION
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\
The project was implemented using Python with OpenCV, NumPy, and Matplotlib.\
\
OpenCV is used to read, process, and save the image. NumPy is used for numerical operations and creating masks. Matplotlib is used to display the original image, red-eye detection, and corrected image.\
\
The program detects the unwanted red color in the selected eye region and reduces the red channel. The corrected image is then saved as an output image.\
\
9.
\f0\b\fs28  RESULTS\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
The project successfully detected the red-eye area in the input photograph and reduced the unwanted red color.\
The output contains three views:\
\
\'95 Original Image \'96 shows the input photograph.\
\'95 Red-Eye Detection \'96 shows the detected red-eye area.\
\'95 Corrected Image \'96 shows the photograph after reducing the red-eye effect.\
\
The corrected image looks more natural than the original image.\
\
